# Fathom — Sensing the dark

The maze is pitch dark. The forager perceives it through what its own light
falls on, what a sonar pulse floods, and what a predator's flare burns. This
file defines the fog of war and its three visibility states, the forager's
light and the brightness that drives it, the sonar pulse, the ink cloud, and
what each enemy effect reveals. It builds on the tile grid in
`specs/overview.md` and the maze in `specs/maze.md`, and the hunters that
answer to the light and the sound defined here are in `specs/predators.md`.

## The fog of war

Every tile of the maze is in one of three visibility states at each instant,
and it is drawn according to that state.

| State | Reported | The tile is |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Unrevealed | `u` | Never touched by the forager's light, a sonar pulse or a flare. Drawn as the flat unrevealed fog `specs/overview.md` fixes, which reads the same over rock as over open water. |
| Remembered | `r` | Revealed earlier and not lit this instant. Drawn dim: rock as dark stone, corridor as faint open water, and any plankton on it as a faint mote. |
| Lit | `l` | Revealed this instant by the forager's light, a live sonar mark or a flare. Drawn at full brightness. |

Three things reveal a tile: the forager's passive light, a sonar pulse's front
as it arrives, and a flare's bloom. A revealed tile is lit while its source
holds it and remembered from then on.

## What is remembered

- Terrain and plankton. Once a tile has been revealed by any source it stays
  remembered for the rest of the current maze, across losing a life included.
  Descending to a deeper maze lays out a fresh maze whose fog is fully
  unrevealed.
- Predators. A predator's body is drawn only while it is lit this instant:
  inside the forager's light, during the window a sonar pulse or a flare shows
  it, or during its own detection alert (`specs/predators.md`). Between those
  glimpses it is not drawn, wherever it stands, and nothing of where it was is
  kept.
{{#if (eq variant.slug "kindle")}}
- The amber lights. The bonus drifter and the Lanternjaw's bulb-light
  (`specs/predators/lanternjaw.md`) are the maze's two amber lights, each drawn
  as a single glowing amber point and drawn alike, so which glimmer is which is
  not readable at a glance. They are clipped to the vision circle below: an
  amber light inside the circle is drawn whatever the fog beneath it says and
  wherever the light pocket fails to reach, and an amber light beyond the
  circle is painted over with the flat fog like the ground around it. Only the
  Lanternjaw's bulb is drawn that way, and its body follows the rule above.
{{else}}
- The amber lights. The bonus drifter and the Lanternjaw's bulb-light
  (`specs/predators/lanternjaw.md`) are the maze's two amber lights, and both
  are drawn at all times and at any distance, across unrevealed fog and through
  rock. Each is a single glowing amber point, drawn alike, so which glimmer is
  which is not readable at a glance. Only the Lanternjaw's bulb is drawn that
  way, and its body follows the rule above.

The whole explored map stays drawn. Every tile ever revealed keeps being drawn,
across the entire grid at once, remembered tiles dim and the pocket around the
forager bright. The tiles drawn black are the never-revealed ones.
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq variant.slug "kindle")}}

## The vision circle

The forager carries an outer vision circle, and the maze is drawn only inside
it.

- Its radius is `R = KINDLE_VISION_MIN + KINDLE_VISION_GAIN * G`, with
  `KINDLE_VISION_MIN` (`192`) and `KINDLE_VISION_GAIN` (`128`) in logical units,
  so `R` is `192` (6 tiles) at `G = 0` and `320` (10 tiles) at `G = 1`, where
  `G` is the brightness below.
- It is a true circle of radius `R` about the forager's center. Terrain,
  plankton and the amber lights are drawn inside it, and its edge runs through
  the middle of a tile as readily as along one rather than being rounded to
  whole tiles.
- It is a rendering mask and it senses nothing. It reveals no tile and
  remembers no tile: what shows inside it is what the fog of war has already
  revealed by another means, at its remembered or lit brightness, and ground
  inside the circle that has never been revealed is drawn as fog.
- Ground beyond `R` is painted with the same flat fog as never-revealed ground,
  and it stays remembered underneath. Returning to it draws it again, dim, with
  any uneaten plankton still on it.
- Predators are not governed by it. A predator is drawn by the light pocket
  below, by a sonar mark, by a flare and by its own detection alert, and the
  vision circle draws none.
- Three things are drawn over the blackout and so show beyond the circle: the
  Flarefish's flare bloom, the forager's own sonar wavefront, and the
  Gloamfin's ping wavefront (`specs/predators.md`).
- A soft glow in the forager's color fills the circle.
{{/if}}

## The forager's light

The forager gives off a soft light, so a pocket of maze around it is always
lit.{{#if (eq variant.slug "kindle")}} It is the smaller of the two circles the forager carries, and it is the
one that reveals and the one that draws predators.{{/if}}

- Its radius is `V = VISION_MIN + VISION_GAIN * G`, with `VISION_MIN` (`96`)
  and `VISION_GAIN` (`64`) in logical units, so `V` is `96` (3 tiles) at
  `G = 0` and `160` (5 tiles) at `G = 1`.{{#if (eq variant.slug "kindle")}} `V` is smaller than `R` at every brightness.{{/if}}
- The light travels straight. A tile is lit by it when the tile's center lies
  within `V` of the forager's center and the segment joining those two centers
  crosses no rock tile other than that tile itself.
- The light reveals the rock it lands on and stops there. A rock tile the light
  reaches is lit and drawn as rock, and the tiles behind it are left as they
  were.
- Predators and plankton inside the lit set are drawn live.

## Brightness

Brightness is a value `G` in `[0, 1]`, `0` when the forager has not eaten
recently.

- Each plankton eaten adds `BRIGHT_PER_EAT` (`0.34`) to `G`, clamped at `1`.
- Eating arms a hold of `BRIGHT_HOLD` (`1.0 s`), in full each time. While the
  hold runs `G` is steady.
- Once the hold expires `G` decays continuously, halving every
  `BRIGHT_HALFLIFE` (`0.9 s`), so a tick of length `dt` takes `G` to
  `G * 0.5 ^ (dt / 0.9)`.
{{#if (eq variant.slug "kindle")}}
- `G` drives both circles, the light radius `V` and the vision circle `R`, by
  the formulas above.
{{else}}
- `G` drives the light radius `V` by the formula above.
{{/if}}
- `G` is what the Lanternjaw and the Flarefish hunt. Each senses the forager
  out to a light detection range that grows with `G`, as
  `specs/predators/lanternjaw.md` and `specs/predators/flarefish.md` fix.

## The sonar pulse

The sonar pulse floods the corridors around the forager, revealing them and
marking the hunters standing in them. The control is in `specs/movement.md`.

- Cooldown. A pulse is emitted when its cooldown is `0`, and emitting one sets
  the cooldown to `SONAR_COOLDOWN` (`1.5 s`), which then runs down. Pulses are
  unlimited, and the cooldown is the only limit on them. The HUD carries a
  readiness gauge (`specs/ui.md`).
- Range. A pulse travels from the forager's tile through open tiles alone,
  following the corridors, out to a path range of `E` corridor steps. `E` is
  `SONAR_RANGE_BASE` (`9`) tiles at depth `1` and shrinks with depth as
  `specs/progression.md` fixes.
- A wavefront, not an instant circle. The front advances at
  `SONAR_WAVE_SPEED` (`14`) corridor steps per second, so it stands `14 * t`
  steps out `t` seconds after the pulse, and the pulse ends once the front
  passes `E`. Each open tile within `E` corridor steps of the origin is
  revealed as the front reaches it, near tiles before far ones, together with
  the rock tiles bounding those corridors, so a flooded passage is drawn as
  corridor and rock rather than as floor alone. The flood follows the
  corridors, so it reaches around corners and through junctions, and it enters
  no space rock seals off.{{#if (eq variant.slug "kindle")}} What it reveals enters memory, so a corridor it
  finds beyond the vision circle is drawn once the circle reaches it.{{/if}}
- Marks. A predator standing on a flooded tile as the front reaches it is
  marked: its body is drawn at its live position for `SONAR_MARK_TIME`
  (`1.5 s`) from that moment, fading out, whether or not the forager's light
  reaches it. A pulse marks the Gloamfin and the Flarefish.
- The amber lights are left as they are. A pulse draws neither the bonus
  drifter's body nor the Lanternjaw's, and it changes neither amber mote, so a
  pulse never resolves which glimmer is which.
- It is heard. When the front arrives at a Gloamfin it hands that Gloamfin a
  fix on the forager, on arrival rather than at the moment the pulse was
  emitted (`specs/predators/gloamfin.md`).
- Presentation. Draw the pulse as a glowing crest that flows outward through
  the corridors, bending at bends and reflecting off rock exactly as the reveal
  does, rather than as an expanding circle. It spreads across many tiles as its
  own overlay, in the cyan tint `specs/state.md` names for a forager pulse, and
  it is drawn in code rather than from a sprite. How the crest is styled is
  yours.{{#if (eq variant.slug "kindle")}} It is drawn over the vision-circle mask, so it
  shows beyond the circle.{{/if}}

## Ink

The forager releases a cloud of ink that blinds the hunters that see. The
control is in `specs/movement.md`.

- Cooldown. A cloud is released when ink's cooldown is `0`, and releasing one
  sets the cooldown to `INK_COOLDOWN` (`8 s`), which then runs down. Ink is
  unlimited, and the cooldown is the only limit on it. The HUD carries a
  readiness gauge (`specs/ui.md`).
- The cloud. A dark cloud of radius `INK_RADIUS` (`80` logical units, 2.5
  tiles) appears centered on the forager and stands for `INK_LIFE` (`3 s`)
  before it dissipates. It stays fixed at the point it was released, and
  everything swims through it at its ordinary speed.
- Blinding. A Lanternjaw or a Flarefish is blinded while its center is inside a
  cloud, or while the segment joining its center to the forager's center passes
  within `INK_RADIUS` of that cloud's center. A blinded hunter drops any fix it
  holds, takes no new one, and wanders until it is clear of the cloud or the
  cloud expires.
- An ink cloud has no effect on the Gloamfin (`specs/predators/gloamfin.md`).

## What the enemy effects reveal

The two enemy effects that spread across the maze differ in what they give the
forager.

- The Flarefish's flare reveals. Its bloom lights the full disc of the flare
  radius `specs/predators/flarefish.md` fixes around the Flarefish, rock and
  floor alike and straight through rock, revealing and remembering every tile
  in it and drawing any predator or drifter inside it live. The disc is stuck
  to the Flarefish and moves with it, and it is drawn at full brightness for as
  long as the bloom burns.
{{#if (eq variant.slug "kindle")}}
  It is full vision, so it draws even ground that has never been explored, and
  it is drawn over the vision-circle mask, so a flare beyond the circle still
  reads. When the bloom ends the disc goes with it: everything it lit that lies
  outside the vision circle is painted back to the flat fog, still remembered
  underneath.
{{else}}
  When the bloom ends the disc drops from lit back to remembered dim, and the
  tiles it lit stay revealed.
{{/if}}
- The Gloamfin's ping reveals nothing. Its wavefront is drawn sweeping outward
  through the corridors{{#if (eq variant.slug "kindle")}}, beyond the vision circle included{{/if}}, in the tint `specs/predators/gloamfin.md`
  fixes for the ping that cast it. It draws no tile, reveals and remembers no
  tile, and marks no predator and no drifter, the Gloamfin that cast it
  included.
